# G031 — CD Key Generator

*v2. See `cd-key-generator.md` for prose: self-verifying tokens
(the key carries its own proof), checksum as one-way function
embedded in the token, no database needed because the artifact IS
the proof, independent nondeterminism with embedded determinism.*

---

## Choreographic Case: Agent Authorisation Token

[agent-auth-token @agent @capability
    IN ORDER TO
        mint a self-verifying token that any gate can check offline
        without consulting a central registry
        because the checksum inside the token proves its own validity

    @token <- [cd-key[generate
                        {namespace: "capability",
                         data: {agent: @agent, capability: @capability}}]]

    [agent[deliver {token: @token, to: @agent}]]

    ;; Later, a remote gate verifies:
    -> [cd-key[validate {token: @token}]]
       where valid is true
         and decoded agent matches caller
         and decoded capability matches operation
       -> #authorised
       otherwise
       -> #invalid-or-forged
]

---

## Verb Surface

[cd-key
    generate           {namespace, data}          ;; -> key with embedded checksum
    validate           {token}                     ;; -> {valid, decoded}
    decode             {token}                     ;; -> {namespace, data} | #invalid
]

---

## Distinctive Innate idiom: self-verifying `where` checksum embedded in the artifact

[cd-key[generate {namespace: @ns, data: @d}]
    IN ORDER TO
        produce a token whose structural integrity is checkable without
        looking up anything else — the token IS the proof

    @data-groups  <- encode (@ns, @d) into 4 groups of 5 chars from charset
    @checksum     <- one-way hash over @data-groups modulo prime
    return @data-groups + @checksum
]

[cd-key[validate {token: @t}]
    split @t into 4 data groups + 1 checksum group
    recompute checksum from the 4 data groups
    where recomputed checksum is equal to the 5th group
        -> {valid: true, decoded: parse @data-groups}
    otherwise
        -> {valid: false}
]

No database. No callback. No remote authority. The validator does
NOT need access to the issuer — the artifact's own structure
vouches for its integrity. Same primitive every real license key,
airline ticket number, and IBAN uses.

## Distinctive Innate idiom: nondeterministic data + deterministic proof

[cd-key[generate]
    the 4 data groups are randomly chosen (nondeterministic)
    the 5th group is a deterministic function of the first 4
    IN ORDER TO
        combine agent autonomy (nondeterminism, G024) with
        structural verifiability (the embedded checksum)
        so agents can mint tokens independently but all tokens
        pass the same validator
]

---

## Demo

[demo
    @token <- [cd-key[generate
                        {namespace: "capability",
                         data: {agent: "kathryn",
                                capability: "finance-read"}}]]
    ;; -> e.g. "H4K2P-M9NQR-A2X7L-B1VYZ-WQKFP"

    -> [cd-key[validate {token: @token}]]
    ;; -> {valid: true, decoded: {agent: "kathryn", ...}}

    -> [cd-key[validate {token: "H4K2P-M9NQR-A2X7L-B1VYZ-AAAAA"}]]
    ;; -> {valid: false}  (checksum mismatch)
]
